{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Az4matBE98UZ8G8DJujm7M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge from reference behavior on edge cases, breaking scripts and pipelines. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via an AI orchestrator, and verifies parity through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) built around:\n- `docs/` — PRDs, use cases, test suites (specification repository)\n- `cmd/` — per-utility Go implementations\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness (exists in source)\n- `pkg/sys/` — syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` — shared output formatting\n- `magefiles/` — Mage build targets (boundary between human spec work and automated synthesis)\n\n**Current state**: The working branch contains specifications only. Generated code (4,586 LOC) lives at tagged generation-merged commits, not on this branch. `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` exists in source. All release 00.0 use cases have `codestatus: not started`.\n\n**Current release**: **00.0** (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). Four use cases remain:\n- `uc001-magefiles` — not started\n- `uc002-format` — not started\n- `uc003-sys` — not started\n- `uc004-testutils` — **already exists** (source code provided)\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nWithin release 00.0, `pkg/testutils` already exists. The remaining three use cases (magefiles, format, sys) have no Go import dependencies between them. Canonical ordering (P8): magefiles and pkg/ are peers (magefiles doesn't import format or sys). By primary file path alphabetically, `magefiles/` sorts before `pkg/format/` and `pkg/sys/`. Additionally, magefiles is `uc001` — the first use case. Build infrastructure enables verification of all subsequent tasks.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement magefiles -- Build, Lint, Stats:Loc, Analyze (rel00.0-uc001-magefiles)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (magefiles/ component -- responsibility, capabilities, project_structure, and technology_choices for Mage)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find and read the magefiles PRD -- match prd*-mage*.yaml or similar naming)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc001-magefiles.yaml (use case for magefiles build targets)\n      - go.mod (module path and existing dependencies)\n\n    files:\n      - path: magefiles/build.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Build and Lint mage targets -- compile cmd/ packages to bin/, run golangci-lint\"\n      - path: magefiles/stats.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Stats namespace with Loc target for Go LOC and documentation word counts\"\n      - path: magefiles/analyze.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Analyze target for cross-artifact consistency checks on docs/\"\n      - path: go.mod\n        action: modify\n        note: \"Add github.com/magefile/mage dependency if not already present\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement Build mage target that discovers all cmd/*/main.go packages and compiles each to bin/<utility> using go build; create bin/ directory if it does not exist; succeed gracefully if no cmd/ packages are found\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement Lint mage target that runs golangci-lint on all Go source under cmd/ and pkg/; return the lint exit code as the target result\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement Stats:Loc mage target (Stats namespace, Loc method) that counts Go lines of code separated into production (.go excluding _test.go) and test (_test.go) categories, plus word counts for .yaml and .md files in docs/\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement Analyze mage target that parses YAML files in docs/specs/ and checks cross-artifact consistency: verify referenced PRD files exist, verify referenced use case files exist, report any missing or broken references\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Mage targets live in magefiles/ directory with package main per ARCHITECTURE.yaml project_structure; use github.com/magefile/mage/mg for namespaces and github.com/magefile/mage/sh for shell execution\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Build target outputs binaries to bin/ directory at the project root, matching the architecture convention that binaries live in bin/\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Read the magefiles PRD (in docs/specs/product-requirements/) for detailed specifications of each target; follow PRD requirement IDs and acceptance criteria as the source of truth for behavior\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"`mage -l` lists Build, Lint, Stats:Loc, and Analyze targets with descriptions\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"`mage build` succeeds and creates bin/ directory even if no cmd/ packages exist\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"`mage lint` invokes golangci-lint and exits cleanly when no violations exist\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"`mage stats:loc` prints production LOC, test LOC, and documentation word counts to stdout\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"`mage analyze` reports zero errors when all cross-references in docs/ are valid\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"golangci-lint reports zero warnings for all files in magefiles/\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"All targets handle empty directories gracefully -- no cmd/ packages, no pkg/ packages, no docs/ files\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":38193,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_too